  "title": "Few subsequence sums in Z_n x Z_n",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture For every $0 \\le t \\le n-1$, the sequence in ${\\mathbb Z}_n^2$ consisting of $n-1$ copes of $(1,0)$ and $t$ copies of $(0,1)$ has the fewest number of distinct subsequence sums over all zero-free sequences from ${\\mathbb Z}_n^2$ of length $n-1+t$.",
